Negative control for a query failure's MESSAGE being a plain sentence (`S14`).

Puts a `*_title` key back on `DetailedError.message`. Every title in the error
corpus is markdown SOURCE — `503_title` carries its own `**`, and its `_md`
sibling is that same string through the markdown modifier — while an
`Error.message` is rendered as TEXT by every surface that shows it. So the
markup reads out literally on screen, which is what the forced
collection-error preset drew: `Service **temporarily** unavailable`.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the error-handling spec — a failure with no API sentence falls back to a
sentence carrying no markup.

diff --git a/packages/headless/src/modules/query/query.utils.ts b/packages/headless/src/modules/query/query.utils.ts
--- a/packages/headless/src/modules/query/query.utils.ts
+++ b/packages/headless/src/modules/query/query.utils.ts
@@ -378,13 +378,8 @@ export function handleError(
   // Preserve the API's structured error code (e.g. `web_hosting::domain_register_only`)
   // on the DetailedError. Clients that need to branch on it (e.g. domain
   // register/transfer flip) read `apiCode` — message text is locale-dependent.
-  // A plain SENTENCE, never a `*_title` key: an `Error.message` is rendered as
-  // text by every surface that shows it, and each title in the corpus is
-  // markdown SOURCE — so the key reads out its own `**` and the `_md` sibling
-  // its `<strong>`. This one also says what actually happened at any status,
-  // where a 503 title claimed an outage for all of them.
   throw new DetailedError(
-    error?.message ?? t("error.request_process_failed"),
+    error?.message ?? t("error.503_title"),
     status || responseCodes.Service_Unavailable,
     ErrorOrigin.Upmind,
     error?.data,
